examples.question_text:
The graph models an exchange between Australian dollars $d$ and British pounds $p$ on one day.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.5cm,y=0.75cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{conversionBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{gridGrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[step=1,gridGrey,very thin] (0,0) grid (10,6);
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(10.7,0) node[right] {$d$ (AUD)};
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(0,6.7) node[above] {$p$ (GBP)};
\node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,0) {$0$};
\foreach \x in {2,4,6,8,10}{\draw[black] (\x,0)--(\x,-0.08);\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,0) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {1,2,3,4,5,6}{\draw[black] (0,\y)--(-0.12,\y);\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,\y) {$\y$};}
\draw[thick,conversionBlue] (0,0)--(10,6);
\fill[black] (5,3) circle (2pt);
\node[above left] at (5,3) {$P$};
\fill[black] (10,6) circle (2pt);
\node[above left] at (10,6) {$Q$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

(a) Use the graph to convert $8$ AUD to GBP.
(b) Use the graph to convert $3$ GBP to AUD.
(c) Use $P$ and $Q$ to find the gradient. State its meaning and write $p=kd$, leaving $k$ as a fraction.
(d) Use your equation to convert $45$ AUD to GBP.
(e) Use your equation to find the AUD needed to buy $20$ GBP. Round to $2$ decimal places.

examples.solution_text:
(a) Trace up from $8$ AUD to the line, then across to the GBP axis: $8$ AUD buys $4.8$ GBP.

(b) Trace across from $3$ GBP to the line, then down to the AUD axis: $3$ GBP buys $5$ AUD.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.5cm,y=0.75cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{conversionBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{traceRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\definecolor{traceGreen}{HTML}{4F9B63}
\definecolor{gridGrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[step=1,gridGrey,very thin] (0,0) grid (10,6);
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(10.7,0) node[right] {$d$ (AUD)};
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(0,6.7) node[above] {$p$ (GBP)};
\node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,0) {$0$};
\foreach \x in {2,4,6,8,10}{\draw[black] (\x,0)--(\x,-0.08);\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,0) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {1,2,3,4,5,6}{\draw[black] (0,\y)--(-0.12,\y);\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,\y) {$\y$};}
\draw[thick,conversionBlue] (0,0)--(10,6);
\draw[dashed,traceRed,->] (8,0)--(8,4.8);
\draw[dashed,traceRed,->] (8,4.8)--(0,4.8);
\node[left,text=traceRed,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,4.8) {$4.8$};
\draw[densely dotted,traceGreen,->] (0,3)--(5,3);
\draw[densely dotted,traceGreen,->] (5,3)--(5,0);
\node[below,text=traceGreen,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (5,0) {$5$};
\fill[black] (5,3) circle (2pt);
\node[above left] at (5,3) {$P(5,3)$};
\fill[black] (10,6) circle (2pt);
\node[above left] at (10,6) {$Q(10,6)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

(c) $\begin{align*}k&=\frac{\text{rise}}{\text{run}}\\&=\frac{6-3}{10-5}\\&=\frac35\end{align*}$

The gradient is $\frac35$ GBP per AUD. The line passes through the origin, so $p=\frac35d$.

(d) $\begin{align*}p&=\frac35(45)\\p&=27\end{align*}$

$\$45$ AUD buys $\pounds27$ GBP.

(e) $\begin{align*}20&=\frac35d\\d&=20\div\frac35\\d&=\frac{100}{3}\\d&\approx33.33\end{align*}$

You need $\$33.33$ AUD.

examples.question_text:
This conversion graph uses the model $4.5$ litres per gallon.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.45cm,y=0.09cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{conversionBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{gridGrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\foreach \x in {0,2,4,6,8,10,12}{\draw[gridGrey,very thin] (\x,0)--(\x,60);}
\foreach \y in {0,10,20,30,40,50,60}{\draw[gridGrey,very thin] (0,\y)--(12,\y);}
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(13,0) node[right] {$G$ (gal)};
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(0,66) node[above] {$L$ (litres)};
\node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,0) {$0$};
\foreach \x in {2,4,6,8,10,12}{\draw[black] (\x,0)--(\x,-1);\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,0) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {10,20,30,40,50,60}{\draw[black] (0,\y)--(-0.15,\y);\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,\y) {$\y$};}
\draw[thick,conversionBlue] (0,0)--(12,54);
\fill[black] (8,36) circle (2pt);
\node[above left] at (8,36) {$(8,36)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

(a) Use the graph to estimate the gallons corresponding to $25$ litres. Explain why the graph reading is approximate.
(b) Use the labelled point to find $k$ and write $L=kG$.
(c) Use your equation to find the exact number of gallons corresponding to $25$ litres.

examples.solution_text:
(a) Trace across from $25$ litres to the line, then down to the gallons axis: approximately $5.6$ gallons. Line thickness and tracing accuracy limit the precision of the reading.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.45cm,y=0.09cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{conversionBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{traceRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\definecolor{gridGrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\foreach \x in {0,2,4,6,8,10,12}{\draw[gridGrey,very thin] (\x,0)--(\x,60);}
\foreach \y in {0,10,20,30,40,50,60}{\draw[gridGrey,very thin] (0,\y)--(12,\y);}
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(13,0) node[right] {$G$ (gal)};
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(0,66) node[above] {$L$ (litres)};
\node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,0) {$0$};
\foreach \x in {2,4,6,8,10,12}{\draw[black] (\x,0)--(\x,-1);\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,0) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {10,20,30,40,50,60}{\draw[black] (0,\y)--(-0.15,\y);\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,\y) {$\y$};}
\draw[thick,conversionBlue] (0,0)--(12,54);
\fill[black] (8,36) circle (2pt);
\node[above left] at (8,36) {$(8,36)$};
\draw[dashed,traceRed,->] (0,25)--(5.555556,25);
\draw[dashed,traceRed,->] (5.555556,25)--(5.555556,0);
\node[left,text=traceRed,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,25) {$25$};
\node[below,text=traceRed,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (5.555556,-3) {$\approx5.6$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

(b) $\begin{align*}k&=\frac{36}{8}\\k&=4.5\end{align*}$

The conversion factor is $4.5$ litres per gallon, so $L=4.5G$.

(c) $\begin{align*}25&=4.5G\\G&=\frac{25}{4.5}\\G&=\frac{50}{9}\end{align*}$

The exact value within this model is $\frac{50}{9}$ gallons.

examples.question_text:
Graph $A$ converts between two units. Graph $B$ shows the length of a spring as attached mass increases.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{conversionBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{springOrange}{HTML}{EF8B2C}
\begin{scope}
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(3.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(0,3.5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,conversionBlue] (0,0)--(3,2.7);
\node[below left] at (0,0) {$0$};
\node at (1.5,3.7) {$A$};
\end{scope}
\begin{scope}[shift={(5,0)}]
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(3.5,0) node[right] {$m$ (g)};
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(0,3.5) node[above] {$l$ (mm)};
\draw[thick,springOrange] (0,0.8)--(3,3.2);
\fill[black] (0,0.8) circle (2pt);
\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,0.8) {$30$};
\node[below left] at (0,0) {$0$};
\node at (1.5,3.7) {$B$};
\end{scope}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Which graph represents direct variation? Explain using each graph's vertical intercept.

examples.solution_text:
Graph $A$ represents direct variation: it is a straight line through the origin, so $0$ of one unit corresponds to $0$ of the other.

Graph $B$ has vertical intercept $30$ mm. The spring already has length $30$ mm when no mass is attached, so its length is not directly proportional to the attached mass.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{conversionBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{springOrange}{HTML}{EF8B2C}
\definecolor{annotationRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\begin{scope}
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(3.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(0,3.5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,conversionBlue] (0,0)--(3,2.7);
\fill[annotationRed] (0,0) circle (2pt);
\node[below left] at (0,0) {$0$};
\node at (1.5,3.7) {$A$};
\node[text=annotationRed] at (1.5,-0.7) {Through the origin};
\end{scope}
\begin{scope}[shift={(5,0)}]
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(3.5,0) node[right] {$m$ (g)};
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(0,3.5) node[above] {$l$ (mm)};
\draw[thick,springOrange] (0,0.8)--(3,3.2);
\fill[annotationRed] (0,0.8) circle (2pt);
\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,0.8) {$30$};
\node[below left] at (0,0) {$0$};
\node at (1.5,3.7) {$B$};
\node[text=annotationRed] at (1.5,-0.7) {Non-zero intercept};
\end{scope}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
